X6100 IU1WXY firmware: terms of use

Copyright (c) 2026 Giovanni Ricciardi IU1WXY. All rights reserved.

1. What this covers

These terms cover the X6100 IU1WXY firmware: the radio interface program, its
scripts and data written by Giovanni Ricciardi IU1WXY ("the IU1WXY software").
They apply from version 0.128. In the source, the IU1WXY software is every
file with the notice "SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-IU1WXY-Terms", and
every other file of the firmware that has no licence notice of its own and is
not part of the software listed in section 7.

The firmware image also contains software by other authors under their own
licences (see section 7). Those licences are not changed by these terms.

2. What you may do

- Install and use the firmware, free of charge, on Xiegu X6100 radios you own or use.
- Make copies of the image for that purpose and keep backups.
- Pass the unmodified image to other X6100 owners, free of charge, with these terms.

3. What you may not do

- Sell the firmware, or include it in a product or service you sell, without
  written permission.
- Modify, decompile, disassemble or otherwise reverse engineer the IU1WXY
  software, or analyse it (its code, behaviour, traffic or data) in order to
  reconstruct, re-implement or clone it, its algorithms, protocols or data
  formats, or publish works derived from it, except where section 7 or the law
  allows it.
- Copy or imitate, in whole or in part, the visual design of the IU1WXY
  firmware and apps: screen layouts and arrangements, menus and tiles,
  graphic elements, icons, colour schemes and other distinctive parts of
  their look and feel, in any product, firmware, app or website.
- Remove or change the copyright notices, the name or the credits.
- Present the IU1WXY software, or parts of it, as your own work.
- Reproduce the screens of the IU1WXY software, as set out in section 4.
- Reproduce its functions, protocols or names, as set out in section 5.

4. Screens and visual design

The screens of the IU1WXY software are part of the IU1WXY software and are
covered by its copyright: their layout, menus, icons, themes, colours,
graphics, the arrangement of text and the way information is shown on them.

Without written permission you may not reproduce, copy or imitate them, in
whole or in a recognisable part, in other firmware, software, apps, websites,
devices or any other product or material. This applies however it is done:
by copying the code, by redrawing them, by recreating them from screenshots,
photos or videos, or with any other tool.

You may still take and share screenshots, photos and videos of the firmware
running on a radio, to show it, review it, teach it or report a problem,
as long as it is clear that they show the X6100 IU1WXY firmware.

5. Functions, protocols, names and documentation

Besides its code and its screens, the IU1WXY software is made of IU1WXY's
work and know-how in what it does and how it does it: its functions and
features, their combination, their behaviour and operating logic, the way it
controls the radio, its workflows, and the protocols, commands and data
formats it defines (among them the remote control interface used by
X6100 Link and by other programs, the GUI control socket, and its package
formats and their signatures). Its names (X6100 IU1WXY, X6100 Link and the names it
gives to its functions), the manual and every other piece of its
documentation are part of it too.

Without written permission you may not:

- use the IU1WXY software, its documentation, its screens or its behaviour as
  a model, specification or reference to develop, or to have others develop,
  firmware, software, apps, services or devices that reproduce its functions,
  in whole or in a recognisable part;
- implement its protocols, commands or data formats in other software or
  devices, except to use them with your own radio for your own use;
- copy or translate the manual or the documentation, in whole or in part,
  except short quotations with the source given;
- use its names, or names likely to be confused with them, for other
  products or services.

These restrictions apply as far as the law allows. They do not limit the
rights the law gives you that a contract cannot take away, such as observing,
studying or testing how the software works while you use it as these terms
allow, or what the law permits for interoperability.

6. No warranty

The firmware is provided "as is", without any warranty. You use it at your own
risk. IU1WXY is not liable for damage to the radio, to other equipment, or for
any other loss arising from its use. Transmitting is your responsibility under
your licence.

7. Other software in the image

The image contains software under open licences. The main parts:

| Software | Licence | Your rights |
|---|---|---|
| Linux kernel 6.1.82 with the X6100 patches and configuration, rtl8723bu WiFi driver with our patches, BusyBox 1.36.1, U-Boot 2026.07 and the other GPL-2.0 system packages | GPL-2.0 (some GPL-2.0+) | full source at the address below |
| libsstv-denoise.so and its model file (SSTV ML denoiser), libsstv-callsign and libwefax-postproc, all by Hany El Imam 1KO125 (TheMurusTeam, github.com/TheMurusTeam/sstv-ml-denoiser), glibc, ALSA, PulseAudio, GLib, BlueZ libraries, libnm, libsndfile, LAME, mpg123 and the other LGPL libraries | LGPL-2.1+ (LAME: LGPL-2.0+) | linked as separate shared libraries: you may replace them with modified versions and reverse engineer the parts needed to debug such changes; source at the address below |
| codec2 (David Rowe and contributors), used by FreeDV as a separate shared library | LGPL-2.1 | source at the address below |
| JS8 dictionary (js8/dictionary.txt, from JS8Call by Jordan Sherer KN4CRD), a separate data file read by js8ngd | GPL-3.0 | licence and credit in /usr/share/x6ng/js8/LICENSE.js8-dictionary; the file is its own source |
| Pat Winlink client (Martin Hebnes Pedersen LA5NTA), ardopcf (ARDOP modem; Rick Muething, John Wiseman, Peter LaRue) and XARA (VARA HF compatible modem; x0rro), separate programs | MIT and their own licences | licence texts on the About pages of x6ng and in /usr/share/licenses/x6ng/ |
| LVGL 8.3, cJSON (Dave Gamble), ft8_lib (Karlis Goba, with our changes), liquid-dsp (Joseph Gaeddert), Lua, libinput, libdrm, expat, jansson, libxml2 and the other MIT packages | MIT | notices in /usr/share/x6100/licenses/packages/ and /usr/share/licenses/x6ng/ |
| KISS FFT (Mark Borgerding), fsck_msdos (FreeBSD), wpa_supplicant, speex, opus, libvorbis, gpsd and the other BSD packages | BSD | notices in /usr/share/x6100/licenses/packages/ and /usr/share/licenses/x6ng/ |
| OpenSSL 1.1.1, curl, zlib, libpng, Python 3.11, SQLite, Boost, ICU, NSS/NSPR (MPL-2.0), ntp, iw, wireless-regdb | their own licences | notices in /usr/share/x6100/licenses/packages/; MPL-2.0 source at the address below |
| Fonts: DejaVu (Bitstream Vera licence), Montserrat (SIL OFL 1.1), Font Awesome Free icons (CC BY 4.0, font SIL OFL 1.1) | as listed | licence texts in /usr/share/licenses/x6ng/ |
| EiBi shortwave schedule (Eike Bierwirth), downloaded on request | free use and distribution | see the About pages of x6ng |
| Realtek WiFi and Bluetooth firmware (linux-firmware) | redistributable binary | see the package licence |

The radio interface program (x6ng) and the radio control library (x6radio)
are IU1WXY's own code under the terms above and contain no GPL or LGPL code.
Built into x6ng are only the MIT and BSD components LVGL, cJSON, ft8_lib and
KISS FFT, with the fonts and icons listed in the table; their notices are in
/usr/share/licenses/x6ng/ and on the About pages of x6ng. At run time x6ng uses
the shared libraries listed in the table and loads the libraries by Hany El Imam
(libsstv-denoise.so with its model file, libsstv-callsign, libwefax-postproc;
LGPL-2.1+), which stay separate, unmodified libraries: you may replace it as described in
/usr/share/licenses/x6ng/README-replace-libraries.txt.

The licence files of every package in the image are installed on the radio in
/usr/share/x6100/licenses/packages/<package>-<version>/, next to these terms in /usr/share/x6100/licenses/;
the notices of the components inside x6ng are in /usr/share/licenses/x6ng/.

Address of the source code: the Releases page of
https://github.com/IU1WXY/X6100-IU1WXY (file
X6100-IU1WXY-v<version>-gpl-sources.tar.gz). It holds, for each version, the
source of the GPL, LGPL and MPL parts listed above with our patches and build
files, the kernel configuration and the list of upstream source archives
used. The same source can also be requested at info@x6100-link.it.

Nothing in these terms limits the rights those licences give you for that
software.


8. Data sent to x6100-link.it

What the radio sends and why is described in the privacy notice at
https://x6100-link.it/privacy.php.

